      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S022",
      "patient_response": "Well, Dr. Smith, they... my family brought me in. It was because of what happened down at the county fair. See, I was supposed to be giving my talk, and I just climbed right up onto the tractor. It was a John Deere, one of those newer ones... beautiful machine. My granddad used to swear by International Harvester, said the green ones were just overpriced lawnmowers, but the dealership in town closed back in '98. \n\nAnyway, I was up there, and I kept jerking the controls around to show the crowd the new pattern. The pattern is real important, you know? You gotta think about soil compaction, especially with all the rain we had this past April. Mud was up to the axles. But I was showing them the pattern, and I just... I couldn't make myself stop. Even with all those people yelling at me to get down. The yelling just started sounding like the crows out in the south pasture, they get so loud right around dusk...",
