    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Over the past few weeks, have you felt like you had so much energy that you didn't need to sleep much, or felt like your thoughts were moving so fast you couldn't keep up with them?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S036",
      "patient_response": "Well, sleep... sleep's been a funny thing lately. Most nights, I reckon I just doze off for maybe two or three hours, sitting right there in my recliner. It's one of those La-Z-Boys, you know, the brown corduroy ones? Got it on sale over in Shelbyville back when the kids were still in high school. The lever on the side sticks a little, but it's comfortable enough. \n\nBut yeah, two or three hours, or sometimes I don't shut my eyes at all. And the funny thing is, I'm up before the sun even thinks about rising, just feeling completely charged up. Ready to go out and work the whole place like nothing happened. I mean, there's always fencing to mend. The deer, they just push right through the wire down by the creek. You'd think a five-strand barbed wire would keep 'em out, but they find a way. My neighbor, Tom, he put up that high-tensile electric fence, cost him a fortune... but I just don't see the need to spend that kind of money when you can just get out there early and fix it yourself. You know?",
