    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever felt this way—with so much energy and needing so little sleep—at any other time in your life, perhaps months or years ago?",
      "targeted_symptom": "manic_episode_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, let me think on that... you know, looking back over this past year or so, it feels like I've been running on that same high gear for a long time. I'd say these stretches where I'm just charged up, not sleeping, going nonstop... they've taken up about ten months out of the last year. \n\nTen months is a long time to be running hot. It reminds me of back in '82 when we had that drought. The ground was so dry it cracked open like a jigsaw puzzle, and we were hauling water from the county line just to keep the cattle from dropping. Had this old Ford F-250, dual gas tanks, burned oil like nobody's business, but she pulled that water trailer every single day. The transmission finally gave out right in front of the feed store in town. Old man Miller came out, shook his head, and said, \"You work a machine that hard without a rest, something's bound to snap.\" He was right about the truck, of course. We ended up having to rebuild the whole gearbox... took three weeks and cost more than the truck was worth, probably. But you do what you have to do when the cattle need water.",
